hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9736","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: I heard Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said : Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad bin Zurarah told me, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited us in Our house, and he said: “May the peace and mercy of God be upon you.” Saad responded lightly, so I said: Will you not call the call to prayer to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? ! He said: A particle of it, then he mentioned a word that means: He may shower many blessings upon us. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May the peace and mercy of God be upon you.” Saad replied lightly, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May the peace and mercy of God be upon you.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned. Saad followed him and said: O Messenger of God, I was listening to your greeting and I was replying to you in a light way so that you might extend our greetings to us. So he left and ordered He was pleased with a bath, so he bathed, then he was given to him, or he said: They gave him a blanket dyed with saffron and roses, and he covered himself with it, then the Messenger of God was lifted up. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he held his hands while saying: “O God, bestow your blessings and mercy upon the family of Saad bin Ubadah.” Then he ate some food. Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told me, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Asad bin Zurarah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited Saad bin Ubadah greeted him, and when he came to his house, he said: “Peace be upon you,” and the hadith continued. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9737","Muhammad bin Hatim told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya bin Abi told me Many, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Thawban, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Saad bin Ubadah as a visitor, and he said: “Peace On you.” Saad returned the greeting, lowering his voice, and the hadith continued. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9738","Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Muhammad bin al-Munkadir told us, he said : I heard Jabir talking: He went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the religion of his father, so I pushed the door, and he said: “Who is this?” I said: I am, and he said: “I am,” as if he hated that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9739","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja’far, who is Ibn Sulaiman, told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, visited the Ansar and greeted their children, stroked their heads, and prayed for them.”"
"9740","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by boys playing and greeted them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9741","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sulayman bin al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas. “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by boys playing and greeted them.”"
"9742","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to come He visited Abu Talha a lot. One day, a relative of his son had died. He found him sad and asked about him. They told him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “O Abu Umair, what did Al-Naghir do?”"
"9743","Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Khumayr told us, he said: Al-Jarrah bin Malih told us, on the authority of Shu’bah bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, on the authority of Humaid al-Taweel, on the authority of Anas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mingled with us, the Ahl al-Bayt, to the point that He used to say to a brother of mine who is younger than me: “O Abu Umair, what did Al-Naghir do?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9744","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid bin Zuray’ told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to mingle with us and would even say to a younger brother of mine: “O Abu Umair, what has Al-Naghir done?”"
"9745","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mingled with us until he said to a younger brother of mine: “O Abu Umair, what has Al-Naghir done?”"
"9746","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Azhar bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Al-Muthanna bin Saeed Al-Dhabi told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, On the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was visiting us, and he would say to a brother of mine: “What did Naghair do?” to a girl who was his."
"9747","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Muhammad bin Kathir told us, he said: Ja`far bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Raja Al-Ataridi, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man came and greeted me, and said: Peace be upon you, and he responded. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was upon him, and he said: “Ten.” Then he sat down, then another came and said: May the peace and mercy of God be upon you, and the Messenger of God replied to him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “Twenty.” Then he sat down, then another came and said: May God’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon you. The Messenger of God replied to him. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Thirty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9748","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Abu Hani told me, that Amr bin Malik told him, about Fadalah bin Ubaid, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The horseman greets the one walking and the one standing, and the small person greets the many.” \"" 9749"""""
"9749","Muhammad ibn Idris informed us, saying: Adam narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: I was the first to greet the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with the greeting of Islam, so he said: ""And upon you be the mercy of Allah."""""
"9750","Ibrahim bin Al-Mustamir told us, he said: Al-Salt bin Muhammad narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim bin Humaid Al-Rawasi narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, he said: He narrated Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not greet the Jews and Christians, for Greeting them with the palms, heads, and gestures.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9751","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Khalaf told us, on the authority of my nephew Anas, on the authority of Anas, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. In the episode, a man came and greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people, and said: Peace be upon you, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, replied to him. Peace be upon him: “May God’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon you.” When the man sat down, he said: Praise be to God, much, good and blessed praise be to Him, as He loves. Our Lord, and He is satisfied, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “How did you say?” He replied to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as he said, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, ten angels hastened to write it down, all of them eager to write it down, so they hastened to write it down so that They took it to Dhul-Izzah, and he said: Write it as My servant said. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9752","Ahmad bin Sulaiman and Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, saying: Yazid told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said Abdul Rahman: Not Ibn Sirin, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you comes to The people, let them greet, and when they stand, let them deliver, for the first is not more deserving of the afterlife.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9753","Ahmad bin Sulayman Abu Al-Hasan Al-Rahawi told us, saying: Abu Dawud, who is Omar bin Saeed Al-Hafari, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah. Ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in the morning: “We have become upon the nature of Islam, the word of sincerity, the religion of our Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the upright religion of our father Abraham, and what He was one of the polytheists.” Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Qasim, who is Ibn Yazid Al-Jarmi, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say when morning came: the same as it is equal. Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Shababah told us, he said: I heard Shu’bah, saying: I came to Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abi Laila, so I said: Recite to me a chain of narration on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he narrated on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: When morning comes: We have entered the morning on the Fitrah.” So he mentioned the supplication. Shu’bah said: So I went to Salamah and mentioned that to him, and he said: I did not hear from Ibn Abi Awfa. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about this. I said: Not from the saying of Ibn Abi Awfa? He said: No, I said: And you did not narrate from him? He said: No, but I heard Dhar narrating, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that When he said that in the morning, I returned to Muhammad, and in another place in my book, I went to Muhammad and said: Where is my father’s son more faithful than him? Atom? And in another place: Where is a shred of Ibn Abi Awfa’s name? He said: This is what I thought. I said: This is how you deal with suspicion? Abu Abdul Rahman said: Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila is one of the scholars, but he has a bad memory and makes many mistakes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9754","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zannad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aban bin Othman, he said: I heard Othman bin Affan, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No servant says every morning... day and evening of every night: In the name of God, by whose name nothing can be harmed on earth or in the heaven, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, three times if anything will harm Him. Aban was struck by a paralytic limb, so he made the man look at him and said: As for the story, it is as I told you, but I did not do it that day. To carry out his destiny. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad is weak, and Yazid ibn Firas is unknown, we do not know him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9755","Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim Duhaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Fudaik’s hadith, he said: Yazid bin Firas told me, on the authority of Aban bin Uthman, On the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever says in the morning: In the name of God, with whose name nothing on earth or in heaven is harmed, And He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing. No calamity will suddenly befall him during his day, and whoever says it in the evening will not befall him, meaning: no sudden calamity will befall him during his night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9756","Abu Dawud Sulayman bin Saif bin Yahya Al-Harrani told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said Abu Ishaq narrated to us that he heard Al-Aghar, Abu Muslim, say: I bear witness on the authority of Abu Hurairah and on Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, that they said: We We heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The words of whomever he said are truthful to God: whoever says: There is no god but God, and God is great, God Almighty said: My servant has spoken the truth, there is no god but Me, and I am the greatest, there is no god but God, He alone has no partner. He said: My servant has spoken the truth, there is no god Except me, I have no partner, there is no god but Allah, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise. He said: My servant has spoken the truth, there is no god but Me, to Him belongs the dominion and praise, there is no god Except Allah, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah. He said: My servant has spoken the truth, and there is no power nor strength except with Me. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9757","Muhammad ibn Qudamah told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Mujma’, on the authority of Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, he said: I heard Muawiyah, saying “I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he heard the muezzin and said the same as what he said.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9758","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, told us on the authority of Majma bin Yahya Al-Ansari, he said: I was sitting With Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif, the muezzin called the call to prayer and said: “God is greatest, God is greatest.” So he declared the greatest twice, and said: I bear witness. That there is no god but Allah, so he testified twice, and said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, so he testified twice, then said: This is what he told me. Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9759","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mujamma, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, on the authority of Muawiyah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him, when he heard the caller, he would say: “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.” He said: “And I.” When he heard him, he would say: “I bear witness that Muhammad Messenger of God, he said: And I, then he remained silent. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9760","Mahmoud bin Khaled told us, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Amr Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, said: We were with Muawiyah, and when the muezzin said: God is great, Muawiyah said: God is great, When he said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, he said: And I bear witness. When he said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, Muawiyah said: And I bear witness. Then he said, “This is what I heard your Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9761","Mujahid bin Musa told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Amr bin Yahya told me, that Issa bin Omar told him, On the authority of Abdullah bin Alqamah bin Waqqas, he said: “I was with Muawiyah when his muezzin called the call to prayer, and he said as the muezzin said, until he said: He greeted the prayer. He said: There is no power nor strength except with God. Then when he said: Hail the farmer, he said: There is no power nor strength except with God. And he said after That is what the muezzin said, then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say that."
"9762","Ahmad bin Bakkar Al-Harrani told us, he said: Abu Sa’id, the client of Banu Hashim, told us, he said: Abu Harrah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: “My friend Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, advised me to say more often: No.” There is no power nor strength except with Allah, for it is one of the treasures of Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9763","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told me, he said: My father told us, he said: I heard Mansour bin Zazan speaking, on the authority of Maymun Ibn Abi Shabib, on the authority of Qais Ibn Saad, that his father gave him to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to serve him, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by me. I had prayed two rak'ahs, and he hit me with his foot and said: “Shall I not direct you to one of the gates of Paradise?” I said: Yes, he said: “There is no power nor strength.” \Except in God\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9764","Hilal bin Bishr told us, he said: Marhum told us, he said: Abu Naama al-Saadi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a campaign, and when we closed, we overlooked Medina, and the people said “Allahu Akbar.” They raised their voices with it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, your Lord is neither deaf nor absent, for He is between you and the heads of Your souls.” He said: “O Abdullah bin Qais, shall I not direct you to one of the treasures of Paradise: There is no power nor strength except in God?”"
"9765","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Razin, On the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Shall I not direct you to one of the gates of Paradise?” He said: What is it? He said: “There is no power nor strength except in God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9766","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar and Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, saying: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq. On the authority of Kumail bin Ziyad Al-Nakhai, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: While I was walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “O Abu Hurairah Shall I not guide you to one of the treasures of Paradise: There is no power nor strength except with God, and there is no refuge from God except to Him.”"
"9767","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: We preserved it from Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ka’b bin Ujrah, said: I said: O Messenger of God, we have learned how to greet you, so how do we pray for you? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You bless Abraham and the family of Abraham, for You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” Ibn Abi Laila said: And we say: “And we must be with them,” and the hadith stems from (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9768","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: A partner told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Muhib, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of his father, that a man came to the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: How can we pray for you, O Prophet of God? He said: “Say: O God, bless Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham, for You are Praiseworthy and Glorious, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Abraham, you are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9769","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abdullah bin Yahya Al-Thaqafi, trustworthy and trustworthy, told us, he said: Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, On the authority of Othman bin Hakim, he said: Khalid bin Salamah told us, he said: I heard Abdul Hamid ask Musa bin Talha: How to pray for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? And peace be upon him? So Musa said: I asked Zayd bin Kharijah, and he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: O Messenger of God, how is the blessing upon you? He said: “Pray, then say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed the family of Abraham, for You are Praiseworthy and Glorious.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9770","Ishaq bin Mansour informed us, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf informed us, he said: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam. He said: Anas bin Malik told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever prays one prayer upon me, may God’s prayers be upon him ten times.” Ten sins were removed from him, and he was raised ten degrees.” Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the same thing. Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Malali, meaning Abu Nu’aym Al-Fadl bin Dukayn, told us, he said: Yunus told us, he said: he told us Burayd bin Abi Maryam said: Anas bin Malik told me, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a similar matter, and he did not say: “It will be raised to him with it.” “Ten degrees” means like the hadith of Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Yahya ibn Adam, on the authority of Israel, before which it was written inside The part (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9771","Ahmad bin Saad bin Al-Hakam bin Abi Maryam informed us, saying: My uncle told us, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub informed us, he said: Tell me Jafar bin Rabi’ah, that Aoun bin Abdullah bin Utbah said: A man prayed next to Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Asi, and he heard him when he He saluted, saying: “You are peace and from you is peace. Blessed are you, O possessor of majesty and honor.” Then he prayed next to Abdullah bin Omar when he saluted, and he heard him. He said something like that, and the man laughed, and Ibn Omar said to him: What made you laugh? He said: I prayed next to Abdullah bin Amr, and I heard him say the same as what you said. Ibn Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And he said that. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Yahya Ibn Ayyub has reprehensible hadiths, but he is not that strong in hadith."
"9772","Ishaq bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq told us, he said: Muawiyah told us, and he is Ibn Amr, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal On the authority of Awsaja bin Al-Rammah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When he saluted, he said: “O God, You are peace and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honor.”"
"9773","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the salaam during prayer, he did not sit, except for the amount of time he said: “O God, you are the peace and from you is peace. Blessed is this.” \Glory and honor\"""""""
"9774","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told me, my father told me, my grandfather Ibrahim told me, he said: he told me Yaqoub bin Zaid Abu Yusuf, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ “If one of you comes to a gathering where there are people, let him greet, and if he sits with them, then when he stands, let him greet, which makes the first more preferable than the after.”"
"9775","Ahmad ibn Bakkar told me, on the authority of Mukhlid, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan informed me, that Sa`id told him, Qutaibah told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said the salutation: “When one of you comes to a meeting, let him say the salutation. If it seems to him that he should sit, let him sit, then when he gets up, let him say the salutation. It is not The first is more deserving of the last than the last.” The pronunciation is Qutaybah. The newborn disagreed with them (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9776","Al-Jaroud bin Muadh told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, I heard Muhammad bin Ajlan, saying: Saeed Al-Maqbari told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you sits, let him salute, and when he stands, let him salute, for it is not The first is more deserving of the last than the last.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9777","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, saying: Abu Asim al-Nabil al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Zuray’, on the authority of Ruh ibn Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you ends up “The one sitting, let him salute. If he wants to stand while the people are sitting, let him salute. What is better is more deserving of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9778","Amr bin Ali told me, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’ah. On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, borrowed forty thousand from me, and money came to him and he gave it to me, and said: “May God bless You have your family and your wealth, but the reward of the predecessors is praise and recompense.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9779","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, I mostly heard Al-Qattan talking, on the authority of a man from Bani Numayr, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My father is reciting peace be upon you. He said: “Peace be upon you and your father.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9780","Ahmad bin Fadalah told me, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Ja`far bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “He came Gabriel went to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Khadija was with him, and he said: God sends peace to Khadija, and she said: Indeed, God is peace, and peace be upon him. Gabriel, peace be upon you, and may God’s peace and mercy be upon you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9781","Nuh bin Habib told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he greeted her. He said to her: “Gabriel recites his greetings upon you.” She said: May God’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon him. You see what we do not see. Ibn Al-Mubarak disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9782","Muhammad bin Hatim informed us, Hibban informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Aisha, this is Gabriel and he is reciting peace upon you,” she said: I said: May God’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon you. You see what we do not see. You want the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is the correct view, given that Shuaib and Ibn Musafar followed him on that path. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9783","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abd. The Most Gracious, that Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Aisha, this is Gabriel and he is reciting peace upon you.” I said: And upon him be peace, God’s mercy, and His blessings. You see what I do not see. You mean by that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him."
"9784","Ali bin Hajar told me, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, that he heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he greeted you: “When the Jews greet you, one of them says: May peace be upon you, so say: May peace be upon you.”"
"9785","Qutayba bin Saeed and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, according to a reading of it and its pronunciation, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, conveying this to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a Jew or a Christian greets you, he only says: May peace be upon you, so say: \On you\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9786","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the Jews greet, they say: May peace be upon you, so say: And upon you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9787","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that a group of Jews They entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: May peace be upon you. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “On you.” I said: Rather, may peace and curse be upon you. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Aisha, God loves gentleness in all matters.” So I said: O Messenger of God, did you not hear what they said? ! He said: “I said: upon you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9788","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my uncle told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Urwa told me that Aisha said: A group of Jews came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: May peace be upon you. So I understood it, so I said: May peace and curse be upon you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Wait, O Aisha, God loves kindness in matters.” All of it, I said: O Messenger of God, did you not hear what they said? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I said: On you?"
"9789","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: A Jewish man entered the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: May peace be upon you. He said: May peace be upon you. So I understood it, so I said: May peace be upon you. And the curse be upon you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Aisha, you should be gentle, for God loves gentleness in all matters.” I said. : O Messenger of God, did you not see what he said: May peace be upon you? He said: “I said: And upon you.” Imran bin Bakkar told me, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Urwa told me, that Aisha said: A Jewish man entered the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned something similar to it."
"9790","Zayd bin Akhzam told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Anas, that a Jew passed by the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Peace be upon you. Omar said: O Messenger of God, should I behead him? He said: “No, when they greet you, say: And upon you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9791","Ali bin Khashram told us, Issa told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: The People of the Book greet us, so how do we respond to them? He said: “Say: On you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9792","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: The companions of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The People of the Book greet us, so how do we say? He said: “Say: And upon you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9793","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abdul-Hamid, who is Ibn Ja’far, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Marthad, On the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Basra al-Ghifari, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am riding to the Jews, so whoever sets off with me, If they greet you, say: And upon you."
"9794","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who is Ibn Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abu Laila, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, who said: Two men insulted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and one of them became angry, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I know a word that if he said it would make his anger go away: I seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan.” Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Muadh, and the like. Yusuf bin Issa informed us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, Yazid, meaning Ibn Ziyad, informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, and something similar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9795","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz informed us, Hafs bin Ghayath informed us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Sulayman bin Surad, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man, and he mentioned a word, and he became angry and started saying and saying, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I “I know of a word that, if he had said it, what he finds would go away from him: I seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9796","Hannad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Sulayman bin Surad, who said: Two men sought refuge at The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made one of them’s eyes redden and his veins swell, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I know A word that if he had said it, the one who found it would have gone away. I seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9797","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The strong man is not the one who strikes, but the strong man is the one who controls himself when angry.” Shuaib and Muammar disagreed with him"
"9798","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ told us, Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, I am Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, that Abu Hurairah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abd al-Rahman, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Severe is not the same as striking.” They said: What is severe? He said: “The one who controls himself when angry.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9799","Hannad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Saeed, who is Ibn Masruq, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The strong one is not the one who defeats men, but the strong one is the one who defeats himself.”"
"9800","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Hakam informed me, he said: Hajjaj informed us, Ibn Juraij said: Musa ibn Uqba informed me, on the authority of Suhail ibn Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever sits in a gathering in which there is a lot of confusion, then says before He stands up: Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise, there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You. He will be forgiven for whatever he was doing in that assembly.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9801","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Had, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id. On the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not stand in a gathering unless he said: “There is no god but You.” I ask your forgiveness and I repent to you.” I said: O Messenger of God, how often will you say these words when you get up? He said: “No one says them when he gets up from a gathering without being forgiven for what happened in that gathering.” Qutayba bin Saeed disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9802","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, on the authority of a man from the people of Al-Sham, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up from a lot of gatherings, he would say: “Glory be to You, O God And with Your praise, there is no god but You.” The hadith went the same way (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9803","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Salamah Al-Khuza’i Mansour bin Salamah told us, I am Khallad bin Suleiman, Abu Salamah said. And he was among those who were afraid, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat While sitting or praying, he spoke some words, so Aisha asked about the words, and he said: “If he speaks well, it will be characteristic of them until the day Resurrection, and if he speaks other than that, it will be an expiation for him: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, there is no god but You, I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You.”"
"9804","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told me, Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, I am a virgin, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Zuhar, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Imran, on the authority of Nafi’, said: Whenever Ibn Umar sat in a gathering, he would not stand up and pray for those sitting with these words, and he claimed that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray for them to those who were sitting with him: “O God, divide for us from your fear what will come between us and your disobedience and your obedience.” What you bring us to Your Paradise, and what certainty you make the calamities of this world easy for us, O God, grant us enjoyment of our hearing, our sight, and our strength. You kept us alive, and make him an heir from among us, and make our vengeance against those who wronged us, and grant us victory over those who antagonize us, and do not make our calamity in our religion. And do not make the world our greatest concern, nor the extent of our knowledge, and do not impose over us those who will not have mercy on us.” Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ayyub, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Zahr told me, on the authority of Khalid Ibn Abi Imran, on the authority of Ibn Omar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would hardly get up from a gathering without making these supplications. Towards him"
"9805","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No people gathered together and then dispersed before they remembered God except as if they had dispersed over the carcass of a donkey.” \"" 9806"""""
"9806","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: ""Whoever sits in a gathering and does not remember Allah therein, it will be a cause of regret (tirah) for him from Allah. And whoever speaks words and does not remember Allah therein, it will be a cause of regret for him from Allah. And whoever lies down to sleep and does not remember Allah therein, it will be a cause of regret for him from Allah."""""
"9807","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhi’ib, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Mawla Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A people has never sat in a gathering in which they did not mention God except “There was a trial upon them, and no one walked a path in which he did not mention God except that there was a trial upon him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9808","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Ishaq Mawla Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no people who sit in a gathering where they do not mention God except that it is upon them.” A period of time, and no man takes a path in which he does not mention God except that he has undergone a period of time.” Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: Qasim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God bless him and grant him peace: something similar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9809","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, Abu Musab told us, that Ibn Abi Hazim told him. Yaqoub bin Al-Duraqi told us, Ibn Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “A people has never gathered and separated without the remembrance of God except as if they had separated from the carcass of a donkey, and that was the gathering.” \A period of time will be upon them\"""""""
"9810","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abu Amir told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Dhakwan, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no people who sit in a gathering who do not remember God.” Therein, it will be a sorrow for them on the Day of Resurrection, even if they enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9811","Ammar bin Al-Hasan told us, he said: Zafir bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri said: “No people sat in a gathering in which the blessings of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were not prayed for except that there would be sorrow for them, even if they entered Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9812","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Ali bin Suwayd bin Manjuf told us, saying: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No people sat together and then dispersed without sending prayers upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon them.” May God’s peace and blessings be upon him. Do not disperse, smelling of the smell of carrion.” Narration of the hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9813","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, Qabisa told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with him. On her authority, she said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not narrate words like yours. His words were a chapter that he explained, and everyone memorized them.” \He heard him.\"" Abu Osama disagreed with him (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9814","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not narrate the hadith as you do. Whenever he sat, he would speak words explaining it. “Whoever heard it will remember it.”"
"9815","Ubayd Allah bin Fadalah told me, Abdullah bin Al-Zubair told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Mughirah. Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Rabi’ah Al-Walbi, on the authority of Asma’ bin Al-Hakam Al-Fazari, who said: I heard Ali bin Abi Talib say: I was... I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a hadith in which God benefited me in the way He wanted to benefit me, and if he narrated to me anything else, I would swear to him. He swore to me that I believed him, so Abu Bakr told me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Not a servant of He commits a sin and gets up and performs ablution and performs the ablution well, then he prays two rak’ahs, then asks forgiveness from God, unless God forgives him.” Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, Ja`far bin Aoun told us, Mas’ar told us, Harun bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad told me, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ali ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of Asma’ ibn al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, similar to him, and he said in it: He told me Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth: “There is no man who commits a sin” and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9816","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, Sufyan told us, Othman bin Al-Mughirah told me, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Asmaa bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: Whenever I narrated a hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I made his companion swear, and when he swore, I told him the truth, and Abu Bakr told me, and Abu Bakr spoke the truth, in that he said: “No servant commits sin.” So he performs ablution and prays two rak’ahs, then asks God for forgiveness, unless He forgives him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9817","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Asma bin Al-Hakam Al-Fazari said: I heard Ali saying: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, God benefited me as He wished. It benefits me, and if one of his companions narrates to me, I make him swear, but if he swears to me, I believe him, and that Abu Bakr narrated to me, and Abu Bakr told the truth. Bakr, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no believing man who commits a sin, then gets up and purifies himself, and does good.” Purity, then he asks forgiveness from God, unless God forgives him.” Then he recited the verse: And those who, when they commit an indecency or wrong themselves"
"9818","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When a servant commits a sin, a spot is struck in his heart. If he repents and seeks forgiveness and repents, it will be refined.” And if Zaid goes back to it until it closes his heart, then he is the one who mentioned God. No, but he saw in their hearts what they had been earning.”"
"9819","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah. Bin Talha, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Amra, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in what he narrates on the authority of his Lord, Blessed be He. And God Almighty said: “My servant committed a sin, and he said: O God, forgive me.” He said: God, Blessed and Most High, says: My servant committed a sin, knowing that He has a Lord who forgives sins and takes responsibility for the sin, then he sins again and says: O God, forgive me. He, Blessed and Most High, says: My servant committed a sin, and he knew that he had a Lord who forgives sins and takes responsibility for the sin. He said: Then he committed a sin again, and said: O God, forgive. To me, then the Blessed and Most High said: My servant committed a sin. He knew that he had a Lord who forgives sins and punishes sins. Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven. \For you\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9820","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir bin Sulayman told us, I heard Yahya Al-Bahili, who is Ibn Zurarah bin Karim bin Al-Harith Yahya Al-Bahili, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Al-Harith, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was at Arafat, and I said: O Prophet God, ask forgiveness for me, God forgive you, he said: “May God forgive you,” so I turned to the other side so that he could single me out with something over the other people, so I said: Oh Prophet of God, ask forgiveness for me, may God forgive you. He said: “May God forgive you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9821","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarjis, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. So I ate some of his food, and I said: May God forgive you, O Messenger of God. He said: “And yours.” I said: May I ask forgiveness for you? He said: “Yes, and for you,” and he recited: And ask forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9822","Ahmad ibn Abdah informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, he said: Asim informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Sarjis, I saw the Messenger of And I ate with him, and I said: May God forgive you, O Messenger of God. He said: And to you. I said to Abdullah: I ask forgiveness for you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “Yes, and for you.” Then he recited this verse, “And ask forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and women.” Then I turned around until I was behind him, then I looked at the seal of prophecy"
"9823","Abdul Ala bin Wasil told me, Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Nabih, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to us, and my wife called him: O Messenger of God, bless me and my husband. He said: May God bless you and your husband. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9824","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Muslim, and Dawud Ibn Qais, on the authority of Nafi’ Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever says: Glory be to God and praise be to Him, Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You.’ He said it in a gathering of men, and it was like a stamp being printed on it. And whoever says it in a gathering of idle talk, it will be his expiation.” Zakaria told me, on the authority of Ibn Abi Umar, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Muslim ibn Abi Harra, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr, He raises it towards him. Sufyan said: Dawud bin Qais Al-Farra’ narrated to me, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, similarly."
"9825","Ali bin Khashram told us, he said: Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliya, on the authority of Abu Barza Al-Aslami, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would come to the afterlife when the sitting was prolonged, and he would say: “Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, I bear witness.” “There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You.” Some of us said: O Messenger of God, may God bless you and grant you peace, this saying is not ours. Do we hear it from you? He said: “This is the expiation for what happens in a gathering.”"
"9826","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: Yunus bin Muhammad told us, Musab bin Hayyan, brother of Muqatil bin Hayyan, on the authority of Muqatil ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah Al-Riyahi, on the authority of Rafi’ ibn Khadij, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God grant him peace in the afterlife, when his companions gathered to him and he wanted to get up, he said: “Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise. I bear witness that no There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I repent to You. I have done evil and wronged myself, so forgive me. No one forgives sins except You.’ He said: So we said: O Messenger of God, are these words that you spoke to them? He said: “Yes, Gabriel, peace be upon him, came to me and said: O Muhammad, these are the expiations for the assembly.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9827","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ziyad bin Husayn, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah Al-Riyahi, he said: They said: O Messenger of God, what are the words we heard you say? He said: “Words that Gabriel, peace be upon him, taught me, the atonement for sitting: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise, I bear witness that there is no god but You. I ask your forgiveness and I repent to you.” Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Fudayl bin Omar, on the authority of Ziyad bin Husayn On the authority of Abu Al-Aliya (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9828","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ziyad bin Husayn, on the authority of Abi Al-Aliyah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The expiation of the assembly: Glory be to You, O God, and with Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I ask Your forgiveness and I repent to You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9829","Al-Fadl bin Sahl told us, Shuraih bin Al-Numan told us, Muhammad bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maysarah, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered the people and said: “O people, repent to God, for I repent to God in a hundred times today.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9830","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, then Al-Mu’tamir told us, I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “I I will repent seventy times a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9831","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Abdullah bin Raja’ told me, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “I seek forgiveness from God and repent to Him more than seventy times today.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9832","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “I seek forgiveness from God and repent to Him a hundred times every day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9833","Muhammad bin Amir told me, Mansur bin Salamah told us, I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I ask God for forgiveness and repent more than seventy times a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9834","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Abu Salamah bin Abdul told me The Most Gracious, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, I seek forgiveness from God and repent to Him in “Today more than seventy times.”"
"9835","Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Ayyub bin Sulayman told us, Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Atiq, and Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “I seek forgiveness from God and repent more than seventy times a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9836","Muhammad bin Sulayman informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “I ask God for forgiveness a hundred times a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9837","Hashim bin Abdul-Malik told us, Baqiya told us, Al-Zubaidi told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Abi Bakr bin Al-Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “I will seek forgiveness and repent on the day “More than seventy times.”"
"9838","Muhammad ibn Dawud informed us, Ziyad ibn Yunus informed us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Musa ibn Uqba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I seek forgiveness from God and repent to Him a hundred times a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9839","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, Abu Nu’aym told us, Al-Mughirah bin Abi Al-Hurr Al-Kindi told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of his father On the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came while we were sitting, and he said: “I never woke up in the morning without asking forgiveness from God.” \a hundred times\"""""""
"9840","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, Affan told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, Thabit told us, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Al-Aghar, Aghr Muzainah He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “My heart is so ungrateful that I ask God for forgiveness a hundred times every day.”"
"9841","Bishr ibn Hilal informed us, saying: Ja'far narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Burdah, from a man among his companions, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed, a cloud (or veil) comes over my heart, so I seek Allah's forgiveness one hundred times every day."""""
"9842","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah speaking, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, he said: Abu Burdah told me, he said: I sat next to a man from among the immigrants whose humility I admired, and I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: “O people, repent to God and ask for His forgiveness, for I repent to God and ask for forgiveness a hundred times or more every day.” \One hundred times\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9843","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Al-Aghar, he said: One day he said, meaning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Repent to your Lord, for by God, I repent to my Lord a hundred times a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9844","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, Muhammad told us, Abd al-Rahman told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Burdah, On the authority of Al-Aghar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Repent to God, for I repent to Him a hundred times a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9845","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Burdah He said: I heard Al-Aghar, and he was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Repent to your Lord, for I repent to Him a hundred times a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9846","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, Sa`id bin Amir told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muslim bin Nazir, on the authority of Hudhayfah, He said: I said: O Messenger of God, I am a man with a loose tongue, and will this spread to my family? He said: “So where are you when it comes to asking for forgiveness? I ask God for forgiveness today, or he said: a hundred times today and tonight.” Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Muhammad told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, saying: I heard Al-Walid, Abu Al-Mughirah. Or Al-Mughirah, Abu Al-Walid narrated, on the authority of Hudhayfah, something similar. Most of Abu Ishaq’s companions disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9847","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Mughirah, he said: Hudhayfah said: I complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lost my tongue and said: “Where are you when it comes to seeking forgiveness? I ask God for forgiveness a hundred times every day.”"
"9848","Amr bin Ali told us, Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaid Abu Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I was a man who used his tongue against my family, so I said: O Messenger of God, I was afraid that my tongue would put me into Hell? He said: “So where are you when it comes to seeking forgiveness? I ask God for forgiveness a day and repent to Him a hundred times.”"
"9849","Abdul Hamid bin Muhammad told us, Mukhlid told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My tongue burned me, and he mentioned one of his concerns to his family. He said: “Where are you when it comes to seeking forgiveness? “I ask forgiveness from God every day and repent to Him a hundred times.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9850","Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim told us, Omar bin Hafs told us, my father told us, Abu Khaled Al-Dalani told us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mughirah Ubaid Al-Bajli, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I Flirt of the tongue, have I burned my family with my tongue? He said: “So where are you when it comes to seeking forgiveness? I seek forgiveness from God and repent to Him a hundred times a day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9851","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, Al-Walid told us, Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Khalid bin Abdullah bin Al-Hussein, said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: “I have not seen anyone say more often: I ask forgiveness from God and repent to Him, than The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9852","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed told me, my father told us, Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, who is Ibn Irq, told us: I heard Abdullah bin In secret, he says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Blessed is he who finds in his book much seeking forgiveness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9853","Ishaq bin Musa told me, Al-Walid bin Muslim told me, Al-Hakam bin Musab Al-Qurashi told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever seeks forgiveness a lot, God will grant him relief from every worry. And from every distress there is a way out, and He provides for him from where he does not expect.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9854","Muhammad bin Abdullah told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, liked it when he prayed for three people and asked for forgiveness from three people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9855","Amr bin Ali told us, Abu Ali, who is the Hanafi, told us, Malik bin Mughal told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar said: We used to count to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in one sitting a hundred times. He would say: “My Lord, forgive me, and repent.” Ali, you are the Forgiver, the Forgiver. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9856","Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Husayn told us, Zuhair told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I heard him ask for forgiveness a hundred times, saying: “O God, forgive me, have mercy on me, and repent.” Ali, you are the Forgiver, the Forgiver. Zuhair memorized"
"9857","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Khabab, he said: I heard Abul Fadl, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: He was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “O God, forgive me, for you are the Most Merciful and the Forgiving,” so that He counted the instrument in his hand one hundred times"
"9858","Muhammad bin Muawiyah bin Abdul Rahman told us, Ibrahim bin Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, Sa`id bin Ziyad al-Mukhtab narrated to me, I heard Sulayman bin Yassar, he said: Muslim bin Al-Sa’ib informed me, on the authority of Khabab bin Al-Art, he said: I asked The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I said: O Messenger of God, how do we ask for forgiveness? He said: “Say: O God, forgive us, have mercy on us, and repent, and mention a word that means ‘on us’. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.” Muawiyah bin Salih told us, Khalid told us, Saeed bin Ziyad told me, I heard Sulayman bin Yassar speaking, on the authority of Muslim bin Al-Sa’ib bin Khabbab, they said: O Messenger of God, how do we ask for forgiveness? Towards him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9859","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us, Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, Saeed bin Ziyad told me, who is the Mukhtab, the client of Banu Zahra, I heard Suleiman bin Yassar speaking, on the authority of Muslim bin Al-Sa’ib bin Khabab, they said: O Messenger of God, how do we ask for forgiveness? He said: “Say: O God, forgive us, have mercy on us, and turn to us. Indeed, You are the Most Accepting, the Most Merciful.”"
"9860","Amr bin Ali told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal, Yahya bin Saeed, and Ibn Abi Adi told us, they said: He told us Hussein Al-Mu'allim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Bashir bin Ka'b, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “The master of seeking forgiveness is for the servant to say: There is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant. I abide by Your covenant and promise.” I am able, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done, and I acknowledge Your grace upon me, and I acknowledge my sin to You. Forgive me, for only He forgives sins. You, if he says it in the morning and is certain of it and dies, he will enter Paradise, and if he says it in the evening and is certain of it and dies, he will enter Paradise.” Thabit bin Aslam disagreed with him"
"9861","Sulayman bin Ubayd Allah told us, Bahz bin Asad told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, Thabit told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraydah. A group of people accompanied Shaddad ibn Aws, and they said: Tell us something you heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Whoever says in the morning: O God, You are my Lord, there is no god but You, You created me and I am Your servant, according to Your covenant.” I promise you as much as I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your grace upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for it is not... He forgives sins except you. If he dies on that day, he will enter Paradise, and if he dies at night, likewise.” Al-Walid ibn Tha'labah disagreed with him"
"9862","Abdah bin Abdullah told us, Suwayd bin Amr told us, Zuhayr told us, Al-Walid bin Tha’labah Al-Tai told us, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever says when the morning or when the evening dies and dies from that day or from That night, he will enter Paradise. Whoever says: Oh God, you are my Lord, there is no god but You, you created me and I am your servant, and I abide by your covenant and promise. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your grace and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for no one forgives sins except You.”"
"9863","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Kamjar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Munib Al-Abdi told me, he said: We showed On Al-Sari bin Yahya, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Learn, Mr. Asking forgiveness: O God, You are my Lord, there is no god but You, You created me and I am Your servant, according to Your covenant and promise as much as I am able, and I seek refuge in You from evil. What I have done, I acknowledge Your grace upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me my sin, for no one forgives sins except You.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9864","Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, Ibrahim bin Saeed told us, Al-Azraq told us, Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Learn from the master of seeking forgiveness: O God, You are my Lord, there is no god but You, You created me, I am Your servant.” I abide by Your covenant and promise as much as I can. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge Your grace and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me. He forgives sins except you.”"
"9865","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, who said: Abu al-Zinad told me, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioned Friday, and said: “Therein is an hour that no Muslim servant will come to, while he is standing and praying, asking God for anything except He gave it to him.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, motioned with his hand to reduce it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9866","Imran bin Bakkar told us, Ali bin Ayyash told us, Shuaib told us, Abu Al-Zannad told me, from what Al-Araj told us, from what he mentioned He heard Abu Hurairah narrate to him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “On Friday there is an hour that a Muslim servant does not meet while he is standing. He prays and asks God for something, but He gives it to him.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gestured with his hand, clenching his fingers as if he were reducing them."
"9867","Amr bin Uthman told me, Shuraih bin Yazid told us, Shuaib bin Abi Hamza told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyib, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, there is an hour on Friday when no servant comes to ask God for forgiveness unless God forgives him.” \For him"
"9868","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told me, Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Ibrahim bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Rabah, on the authority of Muammar On the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “On Friday There is no hour in which a Muslim servant asks God for anything but He gives it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9869","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Abu Ahmad told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, Abu Huraira: “Indeed, on Friday there is an hour in which no servant of God asks for anything but He gives it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9870","Al-Fadl bin Sahl told us, Al-Ahwas bin Jawab told us, Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ka’b and Abu Hurairah gathered, Abu Hurairah said, the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, on Friday there is an hour of A Muslim joins her in prayer, asking God for good, but He gives it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9871","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, Abu Al-Mughirah told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Yahya told us. Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Rifa’ah bin Arabah Al-Juhani said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When half or two-thirds of the night has passed, God will send down To the lowest heaven, then He says: I do not ask about My servants other than Me. Who is the one who seeks My forgiveness, to whom I will forgive? Who is the one who calls upon Me, I respond? For him? Who is he that asks of Me, that I may give him until dawn comes? The pronunciation is for Isaac"
"9872","Ismail bin Masoud told us, Khalid told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that he heard Abu Kitten, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a third of the night remains, God, Blessed and Most High, will descend to the lowest heaven. He says: Who is the one who calls upon Me, that I respond to him? Who is the one who seeks forgiveness from Me, that I forgive him? Who is the one who seeks out harm, that I may reveal it? \The morning breaks\"""""""
"9873","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq told me, Abdul Wahhab bin Saeed told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Yahya told me Ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Ja`far narrated to us, Abu Hurairah narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a third of the night remains God, Blessed and Most High, descended to the lowest heaven and said: Who is the one who asks for My forgiveness, that I will forgive him? Who is the one who calls upon Me that I will respond to him? Who is he who will provide me with sustenance until the dawn breaks?"
"9874","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, I am Abu Al-Mughirah, Al-Awza’i told us, Yahya told us, Abu Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When half or two-thirds of the night has passed, God, Blessed and Most High, will send down His name to the heavens.” This world, and he says: Is there anyone who asks? Is there anyone who asks for forgiveness? Is there anyone who asks for forgiveness? Until the dawn breaks."
"9875","Muhammad bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Our Lord, Blessed and Most High, will descend when the last third of the night remains, and say: Who will call upon Me, that I may respond?” “Who will ask for My forgiveness, so that I may forgive him, until dawn comes?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9876","Abu Dawud told us, Ya’qub told us, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Abu Abdullah Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Our Lord, Blessed be His Name, descends every night when a third of The last night, and He says: Who calls upon Me, that I may answer him? Who asks Me for forgiveness, that I may forgive him? Who asks Me, that I may grant him?"
"9877","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aghar Abu Muslim, On the authority of Abu Hurairah and Abu Saeed, that they bore witness to it against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I bear witness against them, that he said: “Indeed God, Blessed and Most High, gives a delay until the first third of the night has passed, then He descends to the lowest heaven, and says: Is there anyone seeking forgiveness? Asking: Is there anyone who repents? Is there any need until dawn comes?"
"9878","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, my father told us, Al-Amash told us, Abu Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim Al-Aghar, I heard Abu Hurairah and Abu Saeed say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God Almighty gives respite until The first part of the night passes, then he orders a caller to call out, saying: Is there anyone who asks for forgiveness? Is there anyone who asks for it to be given? \"" 9879"""""
"9879","Suwayd ibn Nasr informed us, saying: 'Abdullah informed us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ): ""That when half the night passes, or one-third of it, He—meaning the Lord—descends, and says: 'Who is calling upon Me, that I may answer him? Who is asking of Me, that I may give him? Who is seeking My forgiveness, that I may forgive him?' Until dawn breaks."""""
"9880","Amr bin Uthman told us, Baqiyya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, God descends to the lowest heaven and says: Is there anyone who asks for something to be given? Is there anyone who asks for forgiveness who will be forgiven? Whoever repents will be forgiven until dawn breaks.”"
"9881","Amr bin Hisham told me, Muhammad, who is Ibn Salamah, told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Ata’, the servant of Umm Sabiya, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the first third of the night has passed, God will descend to the sky world, and he does not remain in it until dawn comes. Someone says: Is there not one who supplicates and his supplication is answered? Is there not one who is sick and seeks treatment and is cured? Is there not one A sinner asks for forgiveness and he is forgiven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9882","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim told us, Ibn Abi Fudaik told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abbas, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God will descend during the middle of the night, He says: Who calls upon Me, that I may answer him? Who asks Me, that I may give to him? Who asks Me for forgiveness, that I may forgive him? So he continues like that until the sun sets? \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"9883","Abu Asim told us, Yahya bin Hassan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Nafi bin Jubayr bin Mutim, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God, Blessed and Most High, descends every night to the lowest heaven. He says: Is there anyone who asks, that I may give him? Is there anyone who asks for forgiveness, that I may forgive him?"
"9884","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Abtar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us to recite the Tashahhud in times of need: “Indeed, praise be to God. We seek His help and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in God from The evils of our own selves. Whoever God guides, none can mislead him, and whoever He leads astray, none can guide him. And I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant. And His Messenger” and recited three verses. Al-Masoudi followed him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9885","Amr bin Ali told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us two sermons: the prayer sermon, and the needful sermon. As for the needful sermon: “Praise be to God, We seek His help and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in God from the evils of ourselves. Whoever God guides, none can mislead him, and whoever He leads astray, none can guide him. “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” Zuhair stopped him. Amr bin Ali told us, Khalaf bin Tamim told us, on the authority of Zuhair, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “If one of you wants to give a needy sermon, let him begin by saying: Praise be to God, we seek His help.” The same is true, or He said: “He alone, with no partner.” Shu`bah disagreed with them, and narrated on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah. Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, saying: Muhammad told us, Shu’bah told us, I heard Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He taught us the needful sermon: “Praise be to God.” The same is the same, and he added to it: He recites three Verses: O you who have believed, fear God as He deserves His fear, and O people, fear your Lord who created you from a single soul, and O you who Believe, fear God, and speak good words. Then he will remember his need. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9886","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, Wahb bin Baqiya told us, Khalid told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Hammad bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us the sermon to the needy: “Indeed, praise To God, we praise Him and seek His help, and we seek refuge in God from the evils of ourselves. Whoever God guides, none can mislead him, and whomever He leads astray, none can guide him. “I bear witness that there is no god but God alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” Abu Ubaidah said: I heard Abu Musa saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: “If you want to connect your sermon with a verse... From the Qur’an, say: Fear God as He should be feared, and do not die unless you have submitted, and fear God by whom you question, and the relatives. Indeed, God is There is a watchman over you. Fear God and speak appropriate words until great victory and after that. Then speak what you need.” Israel gathered them together. Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us the sermon on the needy: “Praise be to God, we praise Him and seek His help.” Then he mentioned something similar to it. And he said: Abdullah said: Then continue your sermon with three verses, and the chain of the hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9887","Mahmoud bin Khalid told us, Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Amr said: Qurra told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Every important matter that does not begin with praising God is more definite.” Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, Al-Walid told us, Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he narrated it similarly. Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Uqail, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, mursal. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9888","Ali bin Hajar told us, Al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Umar, told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every speech that does not He begins at the beginning with the remembrance of God, so it is ambiguous.”"
"9889","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Abi Al-Mawali told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, teaches us istikharah in all matters just as he teaches us a surah from the Qur’an. He says: “If one of you is concerned about a matter... Let him perform two rak'ahs other than the obligatory prayer, then say: O God, I seek guidance from You by Your knowledge, and I seek guidance from You by Your power, and I ask You Of Your great grace, for You have power and I do not have power, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. Oh God, if You know that this The matter is better for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affairs, or he said: In my immediate and future affairs, so ordain it for me, and make it easy for me, then bless me in it. You know that this matter is bad for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affairs, or he said: in my present and future affairs, so turn it away from me. And turn me away from it, and ordain for me what is good wherever I am, then satisfy me with Your decree.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9890","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Asim, who said: Abdullah bin Sarjis said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Peace and blessings of God be upon him, when he travels, he says: “O God, you are the companion in the travel, and the successor in the family. O God, accompany us in our travel, and succeed us in Our people, O God, I seek refuge in You from the turmoil of travel, the depression of a turning point, the turmoil after distress, the supplication of the oppressed, and the evil of “The perspective on one’s family and money” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9891","Ya'qub bin Ibrahim told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, Sa'id told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, when he travelled, he used to say: “O God, I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel, the gloom of an upheaval, and the bad outlook of my family.” And money, O God, you are the companion in travel, and the successor in family and money, O God, expand the land for us, and make travel easy for us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9892","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, Uthman told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of When God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out on a journey, he said: “O God, convey good news, forgiveness and satisfaction from You, in Your hand is good. Indeed, You are over all A powerful thing. Oh God, you are the companion on the journey and the successor to the family. Oh God, make the journey easy for us and expand the land for us. Oh God, I seek refuge in You. From the troubles of travel, and the gloom of upheaval.”"
"9893","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah Al-Asadi, he said: I saw Ali He brought an animal, put his foot in the stirrup, and said: “In the name of God.” When he sat on it, he said: “Praise be to God who has subjected this to us.” We will be devoted to Him, and indeed to our Lord we will return.” Then he said “Allahu Akbar” three times, and “thanks” three times, then he said: “There is no god but You. Glory be to You. Indeed, I have been wronged.” My soul, so forgive me my sins, for no one forgives sins except You.” He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said one day like what I said, Then he laughed, and I said: Why did you laugh? He said: “Our Lord, Blessed and Most High, marvels at His servant’s saying: Glory be to You. Indeed, I have wronged myself, so forgive my sins. Indeed, He does not forgive sins except You, he said: My servant knows that he has a Lord who forgives sins. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9894","Muhammad bin Umar bin Ali bin Muqaddam told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Bishr Al-Khathami, On the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, he said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, traveled, he would ride his camel. with his finger, and Shu`bah passed his finger and said: “O God, you are the companion on the journey, and the successor in the family. O God, increase the land for us. “And make travel easy for us. O God, I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel and the gloom of a turning point.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9895","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem informed us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Musa, he said: Usama bin Zaid informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hamza bin Amr Al-Aslami said: His father accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I heard my father saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “At the top of every camel there is a devil, so when you ride it, pray and do not shorten your needs.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Usama bin Zaid is not strong in hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9896","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, Abu Khaled told us, I heard Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man, He came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanting to travel, and he said: O Messenger of God, advise me? He said: “I advise you to fear God, and remember God with all honor.” When he left, he said: “May God increase the earth for you and make traveling easy for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9897","Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Habban bin Hilal told us, Abu Muhsin told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say to the person: “I entrust to God your religion, your trustworthiness, and the seals of your work.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9898","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told us, Affan told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, I am Abu Ja’far Al-Khutmi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b. Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Khutmi, said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would send out an army and it would reach the farewell obstacle, He said: “I entrust to God your religion, your trust, and the end of your deeds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"9899","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, Al-Layth told me, and Ibn Abi Ayyub told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Thawban, that He heard Musa bin Wardan say: I came to Abu Hurairah to bid him farewell, and he said: Shall I not teach you, my nephew, something that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me? And peace be upon him, should I say goodbye? I said: Yes, he said: “Say: I entrust you to God, whose deposits are never lost.”"
"9900","Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad told us, Ibn Aidh told us, Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, Al-Mu’tim told us, on the authority of Mujahid, He said: I went out on the battlefield, I and a man with me, so Abdullah bin Omar took us on. When he wanted to separate us, he said: I don’t have what I can give you, but I I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “When something is entrusted to God, He will preserve it. And I entrust your religion and your trust to God. And the seals of your deeds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
